# Copy to .forbidden-paths in the repo root.
# One gitignore-style glob per line; `#` comments allowed.
# check_forbidden_paths.py fails closed if ANY tracked (indexed) file matches,
# catching files that were force-added or committed before a .gitignore rule existed.
# A bare name like `exports/` matches at any depth, mirroring gitignore semantics;
# prefix a rule with `/` to anchor it to the repo root.

# Directories that must never be tracked:
data/
exports/
phi/
scan-reports/

# File types that must never be tracked (block outright unless a workflow is approved):
*.dcm
*.pfx
*.key
